<title>GERMANY: Thyssen plans 2.6 bln DM investment.</title>
<headline>Thyssen plans 2.6 bln DM investment.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thyssen AG's supervisory board on Friday approved a 2.6 billion marks ($1.7 billion) investment programme emphasising core businesses, the company said.</p>
<p>Approved investments now in the pipeline stand at 4.3 billion marks.</p>
<p>In the year ended September 30, the company invested 2.4 billion marks, up from 2.2 billion the year before.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150 ($ = 1.501 German Marks)</p>
